<SpacedRepetition id="learningScienceDeck" title="Learning Science Flashcards" algorithm="leitner" boxes="5" baseInterval="1 minute">

<CapaProblem id="ebbinghausYear" dontKnow="true" title="The forgetting curve">
Hermann Ebbinghaus memorized lists of nonsense syllables and measured how quickly he forgot them. In what year did he publish the forgetting curve?
<NumericalGrader id="ebbinghausYearGrader" answer="1885">
  <NumberInput id="ebbinghausYearInput" />
</NumericalGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="spacingEffect" dontKnow="true" title="The spacing effect">
<KeyGrader id="spacingEffectGrader">
Two students each study a word list for one hour. Who remembers more a month later?
<ChoiceInput id="spacingEffectInput">
  <Distractor id="spacingMassed">The one who studied for one hour the night before</Distractor>
  <Key id="spacingSpread">The one who studied in four 15-minute sessions over two weeks</Key>
  <Distractor id="spacingSame">Neither; total study time is what matters</Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="leitnerBoxes" dontKnow="true" title="The Leitner system">
<KeyGrader id="leitnerBoxesGrader">
In Sebastian Leitner's 1972 card-box system, where does a card go when you answer it wrong?
<ChoiceInput id="leitnerBoxesInput">
  <Key id="leitnerFirstBox">Back to the first box</Key>
  <Distractor id="leitnerDownOne">Down one box</Distractor>
  <Distractor id="leitnerStays">It stays where it is</Distractor>
  <Distractor id="leitnerRetired">It is removed from the deck</Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="desirableDifficulties" dontKnow="true" title="Desirable difficulties">
<KeyGrader id="desirableDifficultiesGrader">
Robert Bjork calls some obstacles to learning "desirable difficulties": they slow practice down but improve long-term retention. Which of these is one?
<ChoiceInput id="desirableDifficultiesInput">
  <Distractor id="difficultyReread">Rereading the chapter until it feels familiar</Distractor>
  <Key id="difficultyInterleave">Mixing different problem types in one session</Key>
  <Distractor id="difficultyHighlight">Highlighting key sentences</Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<MarkupProblem id="testingEffect" dontKnow="true" title="The testing effect"><![CDATA[
>>Roediger and Karpicke (2006) had students either reread a passage or recall it from memory. On a test one week later, which group remembered more?<<

( ) The students who reread the passage
(x) The students who practiced recalling it
( ) Both groups remembered about the same

[explanation]
Retrieval is itself a learning event. Flashcards work because they make you retrieve.
[/explanation]
]]></MarkupProblem>

</SpacedRepetition>
